From: Droidloom development build
Subject: [PATCH] libbinder: omit context-manager SID requests in a cell

The shared host kernel can provide private Binder contexts without providing
Android SELinux transaction security contexts. Requesting a security context
for every transaction to the context manager makes the Binder driver reject
otherwise valid transactions with EOPNOTSUPP.

Scope the development compatibility behavior to the DROIDLOOM_CELL marker
inherited from the package-owned init. The host sandbox remains the security
boundary; Android SELinux enforcement is restored separately before the
production runtime is declared secure.

--- a/frameworks/native/libs/binder/ProcessState.cpp
+++ b/frameworks/native/libs/binder/ProcessState.cpp
@@ -236,7 +236,9 @@ bool ProcessState::becomeContextManager()
     std::unique_lock<std::mutex> _l(mLock);
 
     flat_binder_object obj {
-        .flags = FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_TXN_SECURITY_CTX,
+        .flags = static_cast<uint32_t>(getenv("DROIDLOOM_CELL") == nullptr
+                                               ? FLAT_BINDER_FLAG_TXN_SECURITY_CTX
+                                               : 0),
     };
 
     int result = ioctl(mDriverFD, BINDER_SET_CONTEXT_MGR_EXT, &obj);
